# THE LEAK SCAN for the public tree (scripts/ops/publish-public-repo.sh --check). Every copied TEXT file is matched line by line
# against every pattern below; ONE hit fails the publish. The scan is the second gate behind the allowlist: the allowlist decides
# which files leave, this file catches a private word, host or key path that slipped into one of them.
#
# Format: one JavaScript regex literal per line, `/pattern/flags`, optionally followed by `allow: <path> <path>` naming published
# paths where that pattern is expected and permitted (each exemption must be justified in a comment above it). This file itself
# and the allowlist are never scanned (they contain the words by construction).

# the private trading platform: its directories, its arming flags, its arm names
/\bexperimental\b/i
/\barming\b/i
/\bXRH_/
/\bXSOL/
# Robinhood as a TRADING ARM (the chain name alone is allowed: the refuse list covers every chain the bots trade, which is the point)
/robinhood[\s_-]*(arm|book|runner|bot|trading|live|paper|signer|keygen)\b/i
/\brh-(live|signer|keygen|runner|paper)\b/i allow: test/burntickerOps.test.ts
/\bRH_[A-Z0-9_]+/
/\b(xrh|xsol|xbnb|xarc|xsolrr|xsolscalp)\b/i

# local env FILES (.env, .env.local …; `process.env.X` is code, not a file) and the private RPC variable (the public code reads
# BURNKEEPER_RPC_URL / BURNTICKER_RPC_URL only). .gitignore must ignore env files in the public repo too — the one place the name is wanted
/(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_.])\.env(\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)?\b/ allow: .gitignore config/public-repo/overlay/.gitignore test/burntickerOps.test.ts docs/burnticker/deploy.md docs/burnticker/runbook.md docs/burnticker/REHEARSAL-RUNSHEET.md deploy/systemd/mct-burnticker-keeper.service deploy/systemd/mct-burnticker-web.service scripts/load-env.sh scripts/service/run-burnkeeper.sh scripts/service/run-burnticker-keeper.sh scripts/service/run-burnticker-web.sh scripts/ops/install-burnticker-units.sh docs/burnticker/reviews/2026-10-10-pair-curve-blind-1.md docs/burnticker/reviews/2026-10-10-pair-curve-recheck.md docs/burnticker/reviews/2026-10-11-lp-lock-blind.md docs/burnticker/reviews/2026-10-11-pair-forward-blind.md docs/burnticker/reviews/2026-10-11-pair-forward-recheck.md docs/burnticker/TODO-OWNER.md deploy/systemd/mct-burnticker-backup.service scripts/service/run-burnticker-backup.sh test/burntickerBackup.test.ts deploy/systemd/mct-burnticker-web-probe.service scripts/service/burnticker-web-probe.sh test/burntickerWebProbe.test.ts
# (the host's units and entrypoints READ that host's env file by name — load-env.sh is the reader; none of them contains a value)
# (operator docs name the host's env FILE so the owner knows where variables go; they never contain a value — the trading repo's env files are never published)
# (the ops test ASSERTS that the keeper never reads an env file and that the ship script excludes them — the names appear only inside those assertions)
# (2026-10-16 audit F-7: the backup script refuses env files and reads ONE named line of the host's env file, its unit and the owner's
#  to-do say so, and the backup test asserts the refusal; no value appears in any of them)
# (blind review 1 of pair_curve states, as a scope note, that no env FILE was touched — a sentence about the method, no value)
/SOLANA_RPC_URL/

# key material and private key paths
/-----BEGIN/
/\bid_ed25519\b/
/\.pem\b/
# a home directory, in path form and in the dashed form tools make of a path (a temp or project directory named after it); a scrubbed
# path says <home> instead (2026-10-18 prelaunch audit A-32: the operator's account name sat in 40 devnet evidence files)
/\/Users\/(?!<home>)[A-Za-z0-9._-]+/
/(?<![A-Za-z])-Users-[A-Za-z0-9._]+(?=[-/]|$)/
/\/home\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\//
/\/root\//

# generic credential shapes (2026-10-18 prelaunch audit A-32): cloud and service keys by their fixed prefixes, a bearer token, and a
# 40-hex value next to a credential word (a bare 40-hex string is usually a git commit, which is public and pinned on purpose)
/\b(AKIA|ASIA)[0-9A-Z]{16}\b/
/\bgh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}\b/
/\bxox[abprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}/
/\bAIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}\b/
/\b[sr]k_(live|test)_[0-9A-Za-z]{16,}/
/\bsk-(ant-)?[A-Za-z0-9_-]{32,}/
/\bBearer\s+[A-Za-z0-9._~+\/-]{16,}=*/
/(secret|token|api[_-]?key|apikey|passw(or)?d|private[_-]?key|credential|auth)[A-Za-z_]*["'`]?\s*[:=]\s*["'`]?[0-9a-fA-F]{40}\b/i
# a raw 64-byte secret key as JSON, or as base58 (a transaction signature has the same length: a fixture's obviously padded
# placeholder — twenty identical characters in a row — is not a key; a real signature in a fixture must be exempted by path)
/\[\s*(\d{1,3}\s*,\s*){63}\d{1,3}\s*\]/
# (the devnet rehearsal records, 2026-10-10 — the morning run and the pair_curve run: these tokens are devnet TRANSACTION SIGNATURES. scripts/ops/verify-evidence-signatures.mjs
#  checks that every 86–88-char base58 token in these files decodes to 64 bytes and is a confirmed devnet transaction, and that the
#  evidence directory holds no 64-number array and no secret/keypair field — re-run it whenever these files change)
# (indexer-1, 2026-10-12: config/burnticker/fixtures/lifecycle holds REAL transaction signatures captured read-only from the public endpoints —
#  the devnet lock-rehearsal coin's create, migration and register_pool, the mainnet $REHEARSAL create, and a public graduated LaunchLab
#  pool's recent signatures — which test/burntickerLifecycleDates.test.ts replays; signatures, never keys)
# ($DEFICIT launch, 2026-10-13: docs/burnkeeper/evidence/mainnet-deficit-2026-10-13/launch.json and current-status.json's deficit.launch.createTx hold the
#  four MAINNET transaction signatures of the launch (initialize_token, the LaunchLab create, the 3 SOL seed, the baseline attestation), each
#  checked confirmed on mainnet with getSignatureStatuses before this exemption was added; signatures, never keys)
# (operator statement, 2026-10-14: config/burnticker/operator.json line 88 holds the ed25519 SIGNATURE the developer fee wallet made over the
#  statement text — public by design, verified by anyone with scripts/burnticker-verify-statement.mjs; test/burntickerStatement.test.ts pins it; a signature, never a key)
# (round-5 devnet rehearsal, 2026-10-15: the run log and the devnet-round5 evidence files hold devnet TRANSACTION SIGNATURES; every 86–88-char
#  token in them was checked with scripts/ops/verify-evidence-signatures.mjs — 114/114 confirmed devnet transactions, no key-shaped material;
#  base64 "Program data:" and hex "dataHex" lines are skipped by that verifier because their base58-looking runs are slices of base64/hex)
# (round-5 MAINNET upgrade, 2026-10-16: config/burnticker/verified-build.json, docs/burnticker/VERIFIED-BUILD.md and
#  docs/burnkeeper/evidence/mainnet-round5/{README-execution.md,squads-votes-execute.log} hold the three MAINNET transaction signatures of
#  the burn_receipts round-5 upgrade (Squads vault transaction 3: create + approve, approve, execute), read from chain; checked with
#  `node scripts/ops/verify-evidence-signatures.mjs --cluster mainnet --rpc <mainnet RPC> <the four files>` — 3/3 decode to 64 bytes and
#  are confirmed mainnet transactions, no key-shaped material; signatures, never keys)
/\b(?![1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]*([1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z])\1{19})[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]{86,88}\b/ allow: config/burnticker/verified-build.json docs/burnticker/VERIFIED-BUILD.md docs/burnkeeper/evidence/mainnet-round5/README-execution.md docs/burnkeeper/evidence/mainnet-round5/squads-votes-execute.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/mainnet-deficit-2026-10-13/launch.json config/burnticker/current-status.json config/burnticker/fixtures/lifecycle/lockcoin.devnet.json config/burnticker/fixtures/lifecycle/mainnet.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/bounty-2026-10-11/funding.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/mainnet-rehearsal-2026-10-11/rehearsal.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/mainnet-deploy-2026-10-11/deploy.json docs/burnkeeper/devnet-run-log-2026-10-10.md docs/burnkeeper/devnet-run.md docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/burns.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/claim.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/curve-buy-1.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/curve-buy-2.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/curve-buy-3.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/curve-sell-1.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/init-token.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/keeper-loop.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/keeper-once-1.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/launch.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/platform.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/register.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/status.json docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-2026-10-10/twap-trades.log docs/burnkeeper/devnet-paircurve-run-log-2026-10-10.md docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/keeper-crank-1a.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/keeper-crank-1b.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/keeper-once-1a.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/keeper-once-1b.log docs/burnkeeper/evidence/devnet-paircurve-2026-10-10/pair1-crank-graduate.json d